@startuml
title RuleSphere - Communication Diagram\n05. Promote, Rollback and Fleet Convergence | UC-18..20, UC-27
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor #F0ECFF
skinparam objectBorderColor #496477
skinparam ArrowColor #496477
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 60
object "operator : AuthorizedOperator" as User <<actor>>
object "api : ManagementAPI" as API <<boundary>>
object "auth : AuthorizationService" as Auth
object "desired : DesiredActiveState" as Desired
object "audit : AuditEvidence" as Audit
object "distribution : DistributionService" as Distribution
object "node : RuntimeNode" as Node
object "artifacts : ArtifactStore" as Store
object "fleet : FleetConvergenceView" as Fleet
User --> API : 1: promote / rollback(target)\n2: observe convergence
API --> Auth : 1.1 / 2.1: authorize action and scope
API --> Desired : 1.2 [authorized]: verify eligibility and switch pointer
Desired --> Audit : 1.2.1 [eligible]: record actor, from/to, time, reason
Desired --> Distribution : 1.2.2 [eligible]: publish desired-state change
Distribution --> Fleet : 1.2.2.1: record desired version and emission time
Distribution --> Node : 1.2.2.2 *[each active node] <<async>>: notify desired state
Node --> Store : 1.2.2.2.1: fetch exact artifact and dependencies
Node --> Node : 1.2.2.2.2: verify integrity, load and validate\n1.2.2.2.3 [success]: make eligible for new requests
Node --> Fleet : 1.2.2.2.4 <<async>>: report loaded state or load failure
API --> Fleet : 2.2 [authorized]: read desired/loaded state, lag and errors
API ..> User : 1.3: desired-state update / error (not fleet completion)\n2.3: convergence view / access error
note bottom of Node
Failed artifacts are never served.
Already-loaded eligible artifacts continue serving.
In-flight snapshots do not change; no node restart.
Rollback reuses the prior immutable artifact, without cloning.
end note
note bottom of Fleet
100% of active nodes must converge within <=2s
from publication-event emission. Surface lag/failure.
This is a requirement, not a measured result.
end note
legend bottom
  Sequence numbers indicate order; nested numbers identify calls.
  * repeats per node; <<async>> branches do not block reply 1.3.
  [condition] guards a message; routine returns omitted; ..> is a reply.
endlegend
@enduml
